# Static Invariant Guards

The following guards are part of the security contract and must remain runnable without a live
provider or deployment edge:

- `test/security/invariants/lifecycle_direct_state_write_invariant_test.rb`
- `test/security/invariants/csrf_verification_strategy_invariant_test.rb`
- `test/unit/security/standard_csrf_invariant_test.rb`
- `test/unit/security/identity_authority_inversion_guard_test.rb`
- `test/unit/security/webauthn_invariants_test.rb`
- the authentication-method inventory/removal guard tests

The GitHub Rails job runs the complete suite, which includes these guards. The local `bin/ci`
pipeline also has an explicit invariant step. Run affected guards directly during local changes. A failing
guard requires fixing the implementation or recording a reviewed contract change; do not weaken an
assertion, add a broad allowlist, skip the test, or remove the guard to obtain green CI.
